<http://example.org/sen0414/ch24/diagrams> a owl:Ontology ; rdfs:label "SEN0414 ch24 narrative diagrams - ABox"@en ; owl:versionInfo "1.0.0" ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch24_diagrams_abox_v1_0_0" ;
    rdfs:comment "The chapter's authored diagrams as cme:NarrativeDiagram individuals: generated by sen0414_page_data_v2_6_0.py from sen0414_ch24_diagrams_v1_0_0.py, typed by the CME narrative-to-diagram mapping (a module of cme_standards_adoption_v1_3_0.ttl, CME 0.16.0)."@en ; owl:imports <http://example.org/cme/narrative-diagram> .

chx:Diagram_SpeakingAndSavingASentence a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "From a sentence to a WAV file with pyttsx3"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:Workflow ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:ActivityDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 24, Generating Speech and Saving Speech Audio to WAV Files: say() adds text to the queue, save_to_file() adds a file name and runAndWait() does the work" ; cme:elementCount 8 ;
    cme:accompanies "SayQueuesText" ; cme:accompanies "RunAndWaitLoop" ; cme:accompanies "WavFormat" ; cme:accompanies "FirstCallRace" ; rdfs:comment "the passage is a sequence of steps with one test on whether the file is complete that leads on or back to waiting: a workflow"@en .
chx:Diagram_FromAudioToSubtitles a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "From an audio file to subtitle files with Whisper"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:Workflow ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:ActivityDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 24, Speech Recognition and Creating Subtitle Files: load_model() loads a model, transcribe() returns the result and get_writer() writes it as a subtitle file" ; cme:elementCount 7 ;
    cme:accompanies "FfmpegRequired" ; cme:accompanies "ResultStructure" ; cme:accompanies "GetWriter" ; cme:accompanies "SrtListing" ; rdfs:comment "the passage is a sequence of steps in which each call needs what the one before it returned: a workflow"@en .
chx:Diagram_TheLoopOfTheTranscriber a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "The transcriber loop: the script, yt-dlp, Whisper and the writers"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:Interaction ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:SequenceDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 24, Practice Programs: for each address the program downloads the audio, transcribes it and writes the subtitle files" ; cme:elementCount 9 ;
    cme:accompanies "TranscribeLoop" ; cme:accompanies "ThreeFormats" ; cme:accompanies "FailureStopsList" ; cme:accompanies "DownloadCall" ; rdfs:comment "the passage is an exchange between the script, the downloader, the model and the writers in an order that matters - the audio exists before it is transcribed: an interaction"@en .
chx:Diagram_ThePinnedReleaseAndTheNewest a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "A reader installing the release the book pins and the newest one"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:Interaction ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:SequenceDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 24 and Appendix A: the book pins pyttsx3 and openai-whisper to releases and the newest releases behave differently" ; cme:elementCount 8 ;
    cme:accompanies "Pyttsx3Package" ; cme:accompanies "PinnedReleaseTruncates" ; cme:accompanies "PinnedInstallFails" ; cme:accompanies "EspeakDependency" ; rdfs:comment "the passage is an exchange between the reader, the package index and the engine in which the pin and the newest release answer differently: an interaction"@en .
chx:Diagram_TheLifeOfAnUtterance a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "The life of an utterance in the pyttsx3 queue"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:LifeCycle ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:StateDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 24, Generating Speech: say() queues the text, runAndWait() starts the utterance and the events report that it started and finished" ; cme:elementCount 5 ;
    cme:accompanies "SayQueuesText" ; cme:accompanies "RunAndWaitLoop" ; cme:accompanies "SetPropertyQueued" ; cme:accompanies "NoSoundCard" ; rdfs:comment "the passage follows one utterance through the states it is in and names the call or event that moves it from each state to the next: a life cycle"@en .
chx:Diagram_WhatYouCanDoWithTheEngines a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "What a script can do with the engines of the chapter"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:SetOfUses ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:UseCaseDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 24: list the voices, change the rate, save speech as a WAV file, transcribe audio, write subtitle files, read the metadata of a video and download audio" ; cme:elementCount 9 ;
    cme:accompanies "VoiceObjects" ; cme:accompanies "RateDuration" ; cme:accompanies "WavFormat" ; cme:accompanies "ResultStructure" ; cme:accompanies "SrtListing" ; cme:accompanies "InfoDictionary" ; cme:accompanies "DownloadCall" ; rdfs:comment "the chapter lists independent things a script can ask the libraries to do - speak, save, transcribe, subtitle, read, download - a set of uses, not a sequence"@en .
chx:Diagram_TextToSpeechAndSpeechRecognitionAtAGlance a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "Text-to-speech and speech recognition at a glance: six branches"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:TopicAndParts ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:MindMap ; cme:readFrom "chapter 24, the opening of each of its main parts: the text-to-speech engine, saved speech and recognition, subtitle files, downloading, the practice programs and the evidence" ; cme:elementCount 25 ;
    cme:accompanies "TextToSpeechEngine" ; cme:accompanies "SavedSpeechAndRecognition" ; cme:accompanies "SubtitleFiles" ; cme:accompanies "DownloadingVideosFromWebsites" ; cme:accompanies "PracticeProgramsAndAnswers" ; cme:accompanies "EnvironmentAndEvidence" ; rdfs:comment "the chapter classifies one topic, speech by program, by what each part is about and lists examples under each - a topic and its parts, with the one idea that holds for every part stated at the root"@en .
